From 3531455ec158b18ec425082d01eb54d526fb0d61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruben Hakobyan <hruben@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 19:01:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] hypervisor: preserve complete ARM CPU snapshot register
 state

Backport ARM SVE register enumeration and pre-finalize restore ordering with their helper changes. Preserve FPSR/FPCR independently of the legacy vector path, including serialized native SVE and non-SVE roundtrip tests.

Upstream: https://github.com/cloud-hypervisor/cloud-hypervisor/pull/8268
Upstream merged revision: 5c25d82f598433353fc96122afe15cf9bb0aa650
Original backports: 083b41905ea59b335c4f211c4186312e30bbf022, e9d044730524d12e243737a1888767b3edf123c8, 4fc414cc8bc56a4c5275b3dd44610e5c75dfbbd1.
The local FP control correction originated in 270badade6a55f5aeb569008f8fbb87f6ba52bd0 with author metadata Ubuntu <ubuntu@localhost.localdomain>; it is not attributed to the upstream author.

Reorganized from original patches 0008-0011.
Signed-off-by: Ruben Hakobyan <hruben@meta.com>

Also adapt upstream 48834e139e9d1882cdefb6cafa42155a13d173bc (Rob Bradford): require the VM KVM ArmSve capability before finalization, matching initialization. Pass the existing VM reference rather than importing the newer ownership refactor.
